    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract). The full suite is green: 2 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality` derivation from the owner's city, matching the existing pattern for derived owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`, etc.).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a fixed `CITY_REGION` lookup table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a `@Transient getLocality()` getter that returns the canonical region, or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't in the table.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `locality` as a `readOnly` string property on the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator adds it to `OwnerDto` and MapStruct maps it by name (same mechanism as the other derived fields).\n\nThe REST responses for `GET /api/owners/{id}` and `POST /api/owners` now include `locality`, satisfying both new acceptance tests (`NSW` for Sydney, `UNKNOWN` for an unlisted city). The full test suite passes.",
