    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the codebase's established pattern cleanly:\n\n- `getLocality()` sits right alongside the existing derived-string property method (the `SILVER`/`BRONZE` getter) on `Owner`, so a maintainer finds a derived, `@Transient`, computed-from-field getter exactly where they'd expect one.\n- The lookup table is a `private static final Map.of(...)` constant co-located with the getter it backs, with a doc comment pointing to its consumer \u2014 the right scope and the right unit for a fixed, owner-local derivation.\n- `getOrDefault(this.city, \"UNKNOWN\")` expresses the \"or UNKNOWN\" fallback directly; no duplication, no branching sprawl.\n- The OpenAPI schema addition mirrors the adjacent `readOnly` derived fields (same shape, title/description/example/readOnly), keeping the contract consistent.\n\nNothing is becoming a catch-all here \u2014 it's a small, additive, idiomatic extension of an existing convention.",
